{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790957441,"nonce":"tEXbHMGx/WTK6uws1uujklG9Ukg=","title":"Nightly windows-x86_64 cannot link rayzor_gpu.dll: unresolved rayzor_plugin_* host carriers","message":"Since 0e785561 (Fix xgpu generation in release builds), the compiler's default `wasm-runtime` feature builds rayzor-gpu with `webgpu-backend`, which now compiles `xgpu_runtime`. That module calls the host-owned `rayzor_plugin_{string,bytes,future}_*` and `rayzor_plugin_raise` carriers. rayzor-gpu's crate-type included `cdylib`, and Cargo builds every crate type of a dependency, so `cargo build -p rayzor` also links a standalone rayzor_gpu.dll. A Windows DLL cannot leave those symbols unresolved (ELF defers them; macOS got `-undefined dynamic_lookup` in 389695e4), so the link fails with LNK2019/LNK1120 for 13 symbols. Nightly has failed daily since 2026-09-30 (runs 36713381522, 36864149350, 37005198995). The Windows Tests job is unaffected because it builds the compiler with `--no-default-features --features cranelift-backend`, which drops rayzor-gpu.\n\nDecision (user): split the cdylib. rayzor-gpu becomes rlib-only, which is what the compiler embeds and where rayzor-runtime provides the carriers; a thin `gpu/plugin` crate (rayzor-gpu-plugin, library rayzor_gpu_plugin) builds the loadable plugin for pack-rpkg.sh and carries the macOS dynamic_lookup flag. The compiler never links a standalone GPU library. A GPU plugin DLL on Windows still cannot reach host carriers (unchanged: there is no host-export mechanism on Windows).\n\nChecks on macOS: the wrapper dylib exports the identical 1520 symbols as the old librayzor_gpu.dylib (rayzor_rpkg_entry, rayzor_gpu_plugin_init, rayzor_plugin_abi_version included); `rayzor rpkg inspect` shows identical method tables for packages built from either; wasm-pack from the wrapper produces the same 80 exported bindings. In a `cargo build -p rayzor` with default compiler features, rayzor-gpu now produces only an rlib.\n\nAlso fixed in pack-rpkg.sh: wasm-pack's --out-dir/--out-name came after the cargo flags, so wasm-pack forwarded them to cargo and the WASM host build failed.","files":null}]}